---
# The tree's naming rule, enforced by scripts/lint.py rather than by review.
#
# Data members carry m_. Public members do not: a public field is part of a
# type's interface, and a type whose fields are public is a value, not an
# object — CachedThumbnail and the wire-format structs are the shape this rule
# protects. Prefixing those would put a private-implementation marker on a
# public API and make the two cases look alike when they are not.
#
# The prefix is the ONLY thing asserted. Case is deliberately left alone:
# this tree has snake_case members in the mpv plugin (m_mpv_gl, beside
# handle_mpv_event) and camelBack everywhere else, and a Case rule would
# rewrite one of them into the other's style for no benefit.
Checks: '-*,readability-identifier-naming'
CheckOptions:
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.PrivateMemberPrefix
    value: 'm_'
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.ProtectedMemberPrefix
    value: 'm_'
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.PublicMemberPrefix
    value: ''
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.PrivateMemberCase
    value: aNy_CasE
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.ProtectedMemberCase
    value: aNy_CasE
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.PublicMemberCase
    value: aNy_CasE
  # qthelper.hpp is libmpv's example file, still carrying its upstream
  # include guard and upstream member names; it is not ours to rename.
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.PrivateMemberIgnoredRegexp
    value: '^(sptr|node_|container)$'
